course: dictionary
lesson: 12625
title: Dismantling: taking things apart
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Dismantle is a verb. It means to take something apart, piece by piece. Add -ing and you get dismantling, which shows the action is happening, and it can also be a noun in phrases like «the dismantling of».
explain: «Sam spent the afternoon dismantling his old bike.» Dismantling means taking the bike apart carefully, so its parts come off one at a time. Check it: swap in "taking apart" and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Dismantling can also mean ending something, step by step. «The dismantling of the old rules took several years.» The rules were not taken apart like a bike. They were got rid of slowly, one by one. The context shows you which meaning is right.
fact: Dismantle means to take something apart piece by piece.
fact: Dismantling is the -ing form of dismantle, and it can also be a noun, as in «the dismantling of».
fact: «Dismantling the tent» means taking the tent down, pole by pole.
fact: When you talk about a system, organisation or rule, dismantling means ending it step by step.
fact: The -ing ending often shows that something is happening now, or is in progress.
exercise: «Mia is dismantling her toy robot to see how it works.» What is Mia doing? | Switching the robot on | Painting the robot bright red | *Taking the robot apart piece by piece | Hiding the robot under her bed
exercise: «The dismantling of the old rules took several years.» What does dismantling mean here? | Breaking a window | *Ending the rules step by step | Writing new rules | Checking that the rules are fair
exercise: «The crew are dismantling the stage after the show.» Copy the -ing word that shows the action is happening now. | show | *dismantling | stage | after
test: «The workers began dismantling the old factory in June.» What does dismantling mean? | Starting to paint it | Starting a new party | *Starting to take it apart piece by piece | Ending a song
test: «Ben enjoyed dismantling the tent after camping.» What does dismantling the tent mean? | Sleeping in the tent | Washing the tent | Hiding the tent | *Taking the tent down, pole by pole
exam: «The dismantling of the old system was done step by step, not all at once.» What does step by step tell you? | It was a dance move | *The ending happened slowly, bit by bit | Nobody noticed it | It happened very fast in one moment
